%!PS
% SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 EfterScript contributors
% SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
% Scenario: a stroke through a matrix. The matrix is concatenated after
% the path is built and before the stroke, so the geometry stays where
% the user path put it while the line width is read in the doubled
% space: the stroke's CTM is [2 0 0 2 0 0] and its width 1, exactly as
% the second page gets by scaling after building the path by hand.
1 setlinewidth
{0 0 100 100 setbbox 10 10 moveto 90 50 lineto} [2 0 0 2 0 0] ustroke
showpage
newpath 10 10 moveto 90 50 lineto 2 2 scale stroke
showpage
